{
  "description": "R14: each of the 4 views, in light and dark, switches appearance live (same pid and window id) and samples its opaque surface, primary text and accent control within ΔE 3 of the token colours, with screenshots of all 8 states recorded",
  "requirement": "R14 (GPUI Phase 1)",
  "notes": [
    "Expected colours come from design/ubilink-tokens.json via the converter's mapping (theme/mod.rs): surface = color.uiBg, text = color.text1, accent = color.accent. uiBg and text1 are translucent and the panel is blurred, so an 'opaque surface' is uiBg's RGB painted at full opacity (light #fafafc, dark #1c1c1e) and the expected text colour is text1 alpha-composited over that surface (light rgba(0,0,0,.88) -> #1e1e1e, dark rgba(255,255,255,.96) -> #f6f6f6). accent is opaque (#007aff / #0a84ff). The values are written here, not read from design/, so the proof cannot move with the tokens.",
    "Where each sample is is the view's layout, so each view reports a region per sample in its state (view.theme_samples.surface/text/accent, window points, README contract); the colour is the probe's. The surface and accent are region means; the text is the best-matching pixel in its run (glyph cores carry the colour, antialiased edges do not).",
    "Same pid: the probe's own child process is still the one it launched (process: unchanged). Same window id: saved per view before the first switch.",
    "Screenshots go to ~/Library/Caches/ubilink-probe/shots/<run>/theming-<view>-<mode>.png (path printed at the end). Pixel and screenshot steps need Screen Recording: ENV-BLOCKED without it, never a FAIL.",
    "Fixtures give every view real content to theme: a captured link, the ranking corpus, two missing permissions."
  ],
  "setup": {
    "graph": "graph-ranking.json",
    "fixtures": {
      "capture": "capture-ok.json",
      "permission": "permissions-two-missing.json"
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "name": "capture: open",
      "call": "open_view",
      "args": {
        "route": "capture"
      },
      "expect": {
        "route": "capture",
        "shell.visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "capture: window id",
      "call": "window_id",
      "expect": {
        "window_id": {
          "type": "number",
          "gt": 0
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "wid_capture": "window_id"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: set_appearance",
      "call": "set_appearance",
      "args": {
        "mode": "light"
      },
      "expect": {
        "theme": "light",
        "override": "light"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: same process",
      "process": "unchanged"
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: same window, still on capture",
      "call": "window_id",
      "expect": {
        "window_id": {
          "saved": "wid_capture"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "call": "state",
      "expect": {
        "route": "capture",
        "appearance.theme": "light"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: opaque surface",
      "pixel": "view.theme_samples.surface",
      "color": "#fafafc",
      "delta_e": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: primary text run",
      "pixel": "view.theme_samples.text",
      "color": "#1e1e1e",
      "delta_e": 3,
      "match": "best"
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: accent control",
      "pixel": "view.theme_samples.accent",
      "color": "#007aff",
      "delta_e": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/light: screenshot recorded",
      "screenshot": "capture-light"
    },
    {
      "name": "capture/dark: set_appearance",
